# Quality-gate ratchet baseline — Task 9i.
#
# WHAT THIS IS: none of the four checks below (`lint`, `format:check`,
# `check:api`, `test:a11y:ci`) are clean on this branch today. The remaining
# faults are real, known, and catalogued (see docs/a11y/findings.md and
# docs/a11y/contrast-analysis.md — the contrast failures are blocked on a
# design decision about colour tokens that isn't this branch's to make).
#
# A hard pass/fail gate would therefore be red from the moment it merges, for
# reasons nobody who touches CI afterwards caused. That gets switched off, and
# a switched-off gate protects nothing while still showing green.
#
# So instead: each number below is the MAXIMUM fault count its gate accepts,
# measured on 2026-08-20 (see the CI job output for the exact commands run).
# CI fails a gate only when a run's count EXCEEDS the number here. This is a
# ratchet, not a green light — it exists to stop the count going up, not to
# say the count is fine.
#
# THESE NUMBERS MUST ONLY GO DOWN. When a fix lands and a run reports fewer
# faults than the baseline, the CI job says so loudly and tells you to lower
# the number here. Do that in the same PR as the fix, as its own line in the
# diff, so the ratchet tightens instead of quietly having slack forever.
#
# Never raise a number to make a failing run pass. If new debt is genuinely
# and deliberately being accepted, raise the number in its own commit with a
# message that says why — never bundle it into an unrelated change.

# ESLint (`npm run lint`, packages/stencil).
LINT_ERRORS_BASELINE=40
LINT_WARNINGS_BASELINE=4

# Prettier (`npm run format:check`, packages/stencil) — count of files
# `prettier --list-different` reports as unformatted. A large mechanical
# reformat was deliberately NOT done as part of adding this gate (104 files
# landing at once would swamp this branch's review) — see task-9i-report.md.
FORMAT_UNFORMATTED_FILES_BASELINE=104

# API consistency (`npm run check:api`, packages/stencil) — Storybook
# story/docs attributes that reference a prop the component doesn't declare.
API_GHOST_ATTRIBUTES_BASELINE=106

# Accessibility sweep (`npm run test:a11y:ci`, packages/stencil).
#
# Three stories are documented, known-flaky (docs/a11y/baseline-2026-08-20.md
# and this task's own local reruns): their pass/fail outcome can change
# between runs of the SAME code for reasons unrelated to a real regression
# (axe timing/ordering, not a content change). CI reports their outcome every
# run but does NOT gate on it. Every other story's failure is gated normally
# against the baseline below — a genuinely new failure anywhere outside this
# list still fails the job.
#
# If a story on this list starts failing for a real, reproducible reason
# (not intermittently), fix it and remove it from the list rather than
# leaving it permanently exempt.
#
# Task 9j (F-023): implemented docs/a11y/contrast-decision.md — the two
# colour-token decisions plus the accompanying usage-fault fixes (see that
# file's Decisions 1-3). Re-measured on 2026-08-20 in the same environment,
# before and after, via `git stash` on this same branch (not against the
# stale committed raw-a11y.txt): stable failures went 27 -> 6. The remaining
# 6 were not colour faults: components-header--default (already listed
# above as flaky), components-tabs--text-tabs/text-icon-tabs (F-023's own
# scope note — axe flags them, computation gives 21.0:1, a harness question),
# components-textarea--rich-editor-enabled (aria-command-name, not
# color-contrast), and components-progress-bar--default/with-tooltip/
# with-percentage-text (aria-progressbar-name — dda-progressbar's root never
# got an accessible name; unrelated to any token task 9j touched).
#
# Final-fix-wave (F-013/F-050): dda-progressbar's role="progressbar" now
# carries a real aria-label (new `aria_label` prop, defaulted to "Progress"
# so no existing consumer regresses to silence). Re-ran the full sweep on
# 2026-08-20 after the fix (`npm run build-storybook` then
# `npm run test:a11y:ci`): all three components-progress-bar--* stories now
# pass; stable failures went 6 -> 3. The remaining 3 are unchanged and
# unrelated to this fix: components-tabs--text-tabs/text-icon-tabs (I-005,
# still a harness question) and components-textarea--rich-editor-enabled
# (F-051, Quill's own toolbar markup).
A11Y_STABLE_FAILURES_BASELINE=3
A11Y_KNOWN_FLAKY_STORIES="components-header--default components-range-slider--default components-stepper-horizontal-stepper--default"
